---
/* Ported from docs/preview/brand-assets.html (CCWEB2-317 phase 2).
 *
 * Shell extraction only. The eight lockup tiles look collapsible and are not:
 * each names a different file with a different caption, and the page's job is to
 * let a reviewer read the filenames against the images they produce.
 *
 * One line needed a real change. The naming pattern
 * `codecave-{wide|tall}-{size}-…` is literal text, and in .astro a brace opens
 * an expression — `{wide|tall}` would have compiled to a bitwise-or of two
 * undefined identifiers. It is wrapped as a string literal so it renders
 * exactly as written.
 */
import DocPage from '../../layouts/DocPage.astro';
---
<DocPage
  title="CODECAVE — Brand assets (real preserved files)"
  nav="foundations"
  stylesheets={['preview.css']}
>
<style slot="head" is:inline>
  .asset      { display: grid; gap: 0.875rem; padding: 1.75rem;
                border-radius: var(--radius-card);
                background: var(--color-surface-secondary);
                border: 1px solid var(--color-surface-quaternary);
                place-items: center; text-align: center; }
  .asset img,
  .asset object { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .asset-light { background: #F4F4F6; border-color: var(--color-gray-300); }
  .asset-light .pv-meta  { color: var(--color-neutral); }
  .asset-light .pv-label { color: var(--color-brand-800); }

  /* CSS url() reference — the glyph mark as a background image. */
  .mark-css   { width: 6rem; height: 6rem; border-radius: var(--radius-tile);
                background-image: url("../build/codecave.svg");
                background-repeat: no-repeat;
                background-position: center;
                background-size: 68%;
                background-color: var(--color-surface-tertiary); }
  .favicon-css { width: 3rem; height: 3rem; border-radius: var(--radius-control);
                 background: url("../build/favicon.svg") center / 72% no-repeat,
                             var(--color-surface-tertiary); }
  .icon-strip  { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: flex-end;
                 gap: 1.5rem; justify-content: center; }
  .icon-strip figure { margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; justify-items: center; }
  .font-row  { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: 1.25rem;
               padding: 0.875rem 0;
               border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-surface-quaternary); }
  .font-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
</style>

<div class="pv-shell">
  <a class="pv-back" href="index.html">&larr; All foundations</a>

  <header class="pv-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">Brand assets</span>
    <h1>Preserved source files, loaded for real</h1>
    <p>Nothing on this page is redrawn. Every mark below is an actual file from <code>build/</code> or
       <code>assets/</code>, copied byte-for-byte out of the captured evidence and loaded here with
       <code>&lt;img&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;object&gt;</code> or CSS <code>url(...)</code>. If a frame
       is empty, the file is missing — not the styling.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="pv-block">
    <h2>Primary lockup — horizontal wordmark</h2>
    <p class="pv-note">The default site-header and letterhead mark. The chevron glyph is always
       <code>#5F20FE</code>; the wordmark paths are white, so the default pairing is
       white-on-near-black.</p>
    <div class="pv-grid pv-grid-2">
      <div class="asset">
        <object type="image/svg+xml" data="../build/codecave-wide.svg" width="420" aria-label="CODECAVE horizontal wordmark, vector"></object>
        <span class="pv-label">build/codecave-wide.svg</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">vector · 357&times;110 · original repo filename · outlined paths, never live text</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset">
        <img src="../build/logo.png" alt="CODECAVE horizontal wordmark, white text" width="420">
        <span class="pv-label">build/logo.png</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">1024px raster alias of <code>assets/codecave-wide-1024-text-white.png</code></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pv-block">
    <h2>Stacked lockup and glyph mark</h2>
    <div class="pv-grid pv-grid-3">
      <div class="asset">
        <object type="image/svg+xml" data="../build/codecave-tall.svg" width="150" aria-label="CODECAVE stacked wordmark, vector"></object>
        <span class="pv-label">build/codecave-tall.svg</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">vector · stacked lockup</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset">
        <img src="../build/codecave.svg" alt="CODECAVE chevron glyph" width="110">
        <span class="pv-label">build/codecave.svg</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">glyph only · avatar and app-icon mark</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset">
        <span class="mark-css" role="img" aria-label="CODECAVE glyph loaded via CSS url()"></span>
        <span class="pv-label">CSS <code>url()</code> reference</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">same file as a <code>background-image</code>, on an icon tile</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pv-block">
    <h2>Inverse variants — light surfaces only</h2>
    <p class="pv-note">For print and genuinely light third-party surfaces. Do not use these to build
       a light theme; see <a href="colors-theme-light.html">colors-theme-light.html</a>.</p>
    <div class="pv-grid pv-grid-2">
      <div class="asset asset-light">
        <img src="../assets/codecave-wide-1024-text-black.png" alt="CODECAVE horizontal wordmark, black text" width="400">
        <span class="pv-label">assets/codecave-wide-1024-text-black.png</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">black wordmark, violet chevron retained</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset asset-light">
        <img src="../assets/codecave-wide-1024-all-black.png" alt="CODECAVE horizontal wordmark, all black" width="400">
        <span class="pv-label">assets/codecave-wide-1024-all-black.png</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">one-ink printing · chevron flattened to black</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset">
        <img src="../assets/codecave-tall-1024-all-white.png" alt="CODECAVE stacked wordmark, all white" width="150">
        <span class="pv-label">assets/codecave-tall-1024-all-white.png</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">one-ink reverse printing</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset">
        <img src="../build/logo-tall.png" alt="CODECAVE stacked wordmark, white text" width="150">
        <span class="pv-label">build/logo-tall.png</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">default stacked lockup on dark</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pv-block">
    <h2>Runtime and app icons</h2>
    <p class="pv-note">Preserved under <code>build/</code> with their source filenames so packaging
       tooling and future agents can consume them directly. The favicon is shown at three sizes to
       confirm the glyph survives down to 16px.</p>
    <div class="asset">
      <div class="icon-strip">
        <figure><img src="../build/icon.png" alt="CODECAVE app icon" width="128" height="128" style="border-radius:var(--radius-tile)"><span class="pv-meta">build/icon.png<br>1024&times;1024 app icon</span></figure>
        <figure><img src="../build/favicon.svg" alt="CODECAVE brand favicon" width="64" height="64"><span class="pv-meta">build/favicon.svg<br>64px</span></figure>
        <figure><img src="../build/favicon.svg" alt="" width="32" height="32"><span class="pv-meta">32px</span></figure>
        <figure><img src="../build/favicon.svg" alt="" width="16" height="16"><span class="pv-meta">16px</span></figure>
        <figure><span class="favicon-css" role="img" aria-label="Favicon via CSS url()"></span><span class="pv-meta">CSS <code>url()</code></span></figure>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pv-grid" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <div class="asset">
        <object type="image/svg+xml" data="../build/logo.svg" width="320" aria-label="Production site header logo"></object>
        <span class="pv-label">build/logo.svg</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">from <code>codecave.pro/src/assets/images/logo.svg</code> — the inline header lockup</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pv-block">
    <h2>Icon ramp — <code>build/icons/</code></h2>
    <p class="pv-note">The seven square app-icon sizes generated by the brand repo&rsquo;s
       <code>build.sh</code> (<code>icons/</code> on branch <code>development</code>), preserved under
       their original filenames. Shown at native size: the chevron has to stay legible all the way
       down to 16px, which is why the glyph — not the wordmark — is the icon mark.</p>
    <div class="asset">
      <div class="icon-strip">
        <figure><img src="../build/icons/16x16.png" alt="CODECAVE icon, 16px" width="16" height="16"><span class="pv-meta">16x16.png</span></figure>
        <figure><img src="../build/icons/32x32.png" alt="CODECAVE icon, 32px" width="32" height="32"><span class="pv-meta">32x32.png</span></figure>
        <figure><img src="../build/icons/64x64.png" alt="CODECAVE icon, 64px" width="64" height="64"><span class="pv-meta">64x64.png</span></figure>
        <figure><img src="../build/icons/96x96.png" alt="CODECAVE icon, 96px" width="96" height="96"><span class="pv-meta">96x96.png</span></figure>
        <figure><img src="../build/icons/128x128.png" alt="CODECAVE icon, 128px" width="128" height="128"><span class="pv-meta">128x128.png</span></figure>
        <figure><img src="../build/icons/256x256.png" alt="CODECAVE icon, 256px" width="128" height="128"><span class="pv-meta">256x256.png<br>shown at 128</span></figure>
        <figure><img src="../build/icons/512x512.png" alt="CODECAVE icon, 512px" width="128" height="128"><span class="pv-meta">512x512.png<br>shown at 128</span></figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pv-block">
    <h2>Web runtime set — <code>favicons/</code></h2>
    <p class="pv-note">The complete installable-web set from the brand repo, copied byte-for-byte:
       a real Windows <code>favicon.ico</code>, the Apple touch icon, and both PWA manifest icons
       declared by <code>build/site.webmanifest</code>. Take these files as-is for packaging; do not
       re-export them.</p>
    <div class="pv-grid pv-grid-3">
      <div class="asset">
        <img src="../build/favicon.ico" alt="CODECAVE favicon, ICO" width="48" height="48">
        <span class="pv-label">build/favicon.ico</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">multi-size Windows icon · browser tab and shortcut</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset">
        <img src="../build/apple-touch-icon.png" alt="CODECAVE Apple touch icon" width="120" height="120" style="border-radius:var(--radius-tile)">
        <span class="pv-label">build/apple-touch-icon.png</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">iOS home-screen icon · dark ground baked in</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset">
        <img src="../build/favicon-96x96.png" alt="CODECAVE favicon, 96px" width="96" height="96">
        <span class="pv-label">build/favicon-96x96.png</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">raster fallback where SVG favicons are unsupported</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset">
        <img src="../build/web-app-manifest-192x192.png" alt="CODECAVE PWA icon, 192px" width="120" height="120" style="border-radius:var(--radius-tile)">
        <span class="pv-label">build/web-app-manifest-192x192.png</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">manifest <code>icons[]</code> · 192&times;192</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset">
        <img src="../build/web-app-manifest-512x512.png" alt="CODECAVE PWA icon, 512px" width="120" height="120" style="border-radius:var(--radius-tile)">
        <span class="pv-label">build/web-app-manifest-512x512.png</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">manifest <code>icons[]</code> · 512&times;512 · maskable source</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset">
        <span class="favicon-css" role="img" aria-label="Favicon via CSS url()"></span>
        <span class="pv-label">build/site.webmanifest</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">declares the two icons above · glyph shown via CSS <code>url()</code></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pv-block">
    <h2>The four finishes, at review size</h2>
    <p class="pv-note">Every lockup ships in eight sizes (96–1024) &times; four finishes, generated by
       <code>build.sh</code> from the three vectors in <code>src/</code>. The 256px cuts are preserved
       in <code>assets/</code> for review; the 1024px masters are there too. Naming is
       <code>{'codecave-{wide|tall}-{size}-{text-white|text-black|all-white|all-black}.png'}</code>.</p>
    <div class="pv-grid pv-grid-2">
      <div class="asset">
        <img src="../assets/codecave-wide-256-text-white.png" alt="Horizontal wordmark, white text" width="256">
        <span class="pv-label">codecave-wide-256-text-white.png</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">default on dark · violet chevron, white wordmark</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset asset-light">
        <img src="../assets/codecave-wide-256-text-black.png" alt="Horizontal wordmark, black text" width="256">
        <span class="pv-label">codecave-wide-256-text-black.png</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">light surfaces only · violet chevron retained</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset">
        <img src="../assets/codecave-tall-256-all-white.png" alt="Stacked wordmark, all white" width="150">
        <span class="pv-label">codecave-tall-256-all-white.png</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">one-ink reverse · chevron flattened to white</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset asset-light">
        <img src="../assets/codecave-tall-256-all-black.png" alt="Stacked wordmark, all black" width="150">
        <span class="pv-label">codecave-tall-256-all-black.png</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">one-ink positive · chevron flattened to black</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pv-block">
    <h2>Typeface files</h2>
    <p class="pv-note">Real Satoshi cuts live in <code>fonts/</code> and are bound by
       <code>@font-face</code> in <code>colors_and_type.css</code>. Each line below renders from the
       file named beside it — if they all look identical, the binding has broken.</p>
    <div class="pv-tile">
      <div class="font-row"><span style="flex:1;min-width:15rem;font-weight:300;font-size:var(--text-subhead)">Your idea stays yours</span><span class="pv-meta">fonts/Satoshi-Light.woff2 · 300</span></div>
      <div class="font-row"><span style="flex:1;min-width:15rem;font-weight:400;font-size:var(--text-subhead)">Your idea stays yours</span><span class="pv-meta">fonts/Satoshi-Regular.woff2 · 400 · production body</span></div>
      <div class="font-row"><span style="flex:1;min-width:15rem;font-weight:500;font-size:var(--text-subhead)">Your idea stays yours</span><span class="pv-meta">fonts/Satoshi-Medium.woff2 · 500</span></div>
      <div class="font-row"><span style="flex:1;min-width:15rem;font-weight:700;font-size:var(--text-subhead)">Your idea stays yours</span><span class="pv-meta">fonts/Satoshi-Bold.woff2 · 700 · production headings</span></div>
      <div class="font-row"><span style="flex:1;min-width:15rem;font-weight:900;font-size:var(--text-subhead)">Your idea stays yours</span><span class="pv-meta">fonts/Satoshi-Black.woff2 · 900</span></div>
      <div class="font-row"><span style="flex:1;min-width:15rem;font-style:italic;font-size:var(--text-subhead)">Your idea stays yours</span><span class="pv-meta">fonts/Satoshi-Italic.woff2 · 400 italic</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pv-warn" style="margin-top:1.5rem"><strong>Known defect, carried forward.</strong> The
      wordmark artwork predates Satoshi and is still drawn in outlined Montserrat Bold. The paths are
      outlined vector, not live text, and must never be re-typed by hand.</p>
  </section>
</div>

</DocPage>
